# Line endings are part of the contract here, so they are pinned rather than
# left to a clone's `core.autocrlf`.
#
# `tests/parity/fixtures/` is a byte-for-byte copy of fancy-flow-php's golden
# fixtures, and `test_parity_fixtures_match_the_source` compares the two
# runtimes' copies as bytes. On Windows, a fresh clone with the default
# autocrlf rewrote every LF to CRLF on checkout — so all 23 fixtures reported as
# "changed between the runtimes" on a clone that had changed nothing.
#
# That failure is indistinguishable from a real divergence, which is the whole
# problem: the test exists to catch one side editing a golden, and a line-ending
# conversion makes it cry wolf on every Windows checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
